  "text": "In this cross-sectional survey of 262 pregnant women coming for their regular clinical visits in one center in Switzerland, we found a prevalence of tobacco products at 7.6%, ENDS at 0.8%, NRT at 0.4%, and cannabinoid use at 3.8%. These findings are in line with those of previous Swiss surveys on tobacco use in pregnancy 46–48. For ENDS, NRT, and cannabinoid use, comparable Swiss data are sparse: the low prevalence of ENDS and NRT use observed in our study contrasts with the marked increase in ENDS use reported among pregnant women in the USA 25, and the 3.8% cannabinoid use was considerably lower than the approximately 20% of pregnant women reporting use of CBD-containing products in the USA and Canada 26 and the 7.9% cannabis use reported in the USA in 2022 28."
}

